      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I suspect that VRChat isn't architectured for low latency. Back on dial up I think latency was 250-500ms, meanwhile VRChat states 100ms latency, but when I do a test of having a person throw up an object and I try and throw another object at it, the views are wildly different. I closely miss, because bad aim, but from the other person's perspective I didn't throw until their object hit the ground. For throwing objects around it seems like there is an owner of the object so it's most interesting to pick up and drop an object and then have someone move it with an object collision.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-04-09T22:37:42.764Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Will the game's ability syncing ability improve in the future? Even if we could squeeze 15 to 20% more would make a big difference overall.\n\nVrchat seems to compare to old gen pc online shooters, where they feel like there is a delay in hit rate with a second or two, let's say you hide behind a door for little more than a second and half the game catches up, and then you get shot.\n\n \n\nThanks for reading.",
